1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Every token launch asks you to trust that something is underneath the price. Usually, nothing is.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:20,000
This is Ballast: a Meteora launch with a floor you can see before the first public trade, and verify yourself.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:32,000
When a creator launches, Ballast computes the floor, F, from the launch parameters alone, and records it on-chain before anyone else can trade.

4
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Every buyer sees their worst case up front. Here: 74% below the curve's final price, down to the floor.

5
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Buyers trade on Meteora's Dynamic Bonding Curve. At graduation, 85% of the raise migrates into DAMM v2 as two positions locked for good, owned by our program.

6
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:15,000
The other 15%, the migration fee, goes into a program vault and becomes a single DLMM limit order resting at F. Three Meteora products, one invariant.

7
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Now we sell everything. Every token holders have. The price slides down the pool's curve, lands on the floor, and the bid absorbs the rest.

8
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:43,000
The worst fill of the whole sell-out: 0.998 of F, fees included.

9
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:55,000
This isn't a promise from a team. It's liquidity and a limit order, and the program has no instruction that withdraws them.

10
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Don't trust our app. One command reads the raw accounts and recomputes F with the same tested library.

11
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:20,000
It checks F against the vault, the bid and the locked liquidity. Sixteen checks. Same answer, for anyone, every time.

12
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:38,000
[FILL: the traction line you recorded, real numbers only] And the challenge is open: break the floor.

13
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Buyers know their worst case before they buy. Creators launch without being called a rug.

14
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Any DBC launchpad can offer it with one config and one instruction. Ballast. Launch with a floor.
